        "publish_date": "1998",
        "description": {
          "type": "/type/text",
          "value": "\"Gordon MacKenzie worked at Hallmark Cards for thirty years, where he inspired his colleagues to slip the bonds of Corporate Normalcy and rise to orbit - to a mode of dreaming, daring, and doing above and beyond the rubber-stamp confines of the administrative mind-set. In his deeply funny book, exuberantly illustrated in full color, he shares lessons on awakening and fostering creative genius. He teaches how to emerge from the \"giant hairball\"--That tangled, impenetrable mass of rules, and systems, based on what worked in the past and which can lead to mediocrity in the present.\"--Jacket."
        },
